.SH NAME
gyro-s3-alerts-set - Set the fill alert of a bucket


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro s3 alerts set   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the fill alert of a bucket

.PP
Sets or replaces the threshold (the alert re-arms). If the bucket is already above it, the e-mail is sent within ~5 minutes. \fBtype\fR percent (1-100, of the package size) or gb (1 to the package size). Errors: 422 \fBtool_action_failed\fR with a message in the account language. A \fBfill alert\fP sends one e-mail to the account address when a bucket's usage reaches the threshold: \fBpercent\fR = a share of the package size (every bucket of the service shares the package) or \fBgb\fR = an absolute size. Checked every 5 minutes. After the e-mail the alert is \fBtriggered\fR; it re-arms when usage drops below 95% of the threshold, and the next crossing sends again. The alert only informs, uploads are not stopped. The package-wide 80% / 100% e-mails stay as they are. Object Storage and Protected Storage (old versions and delete markers count as usage).

.PP
API: PUT /cloud/storage/{id}/buckets/{bucket}/alert (operationId setStorageBucketAlert, scope services_write)


